course: dictionary
lesson: 5809
title: Words for people who judge
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A magistrate is a person who acts as a judge in a local court. In England and Wales, most criminal cases start in a magistrates' court. Context helps you see this: «The magistrate fined him» shows that the magistrate decides a punishment, so a magistrate is the one who judges.
explain: Magistrates usually hear less serious crimes. They are ordinary local people, often volunteers called Justices of the Peace (JPs), not trained lawyers. The clue «only give short prison sentences of months, not years» tells you they cannot give very long punishments.
explain: Watch out for stories. In «The Wind in the Willows», Toad is tried by magistrates and given twenty years. The lesson tells you this could not really happen, because magistrates cannot give such long sentences. Always check a story against what you know about real life.
fact: A magistrate is a judge in a local court who deals with less serious crimes.
fact: «Magistrates' court» is the local court where many criminal cases in England and Wales begin.
fact: A volunteer magistrate is also called a Justice of the Peace, or JP.
fact: Serious cases go to a higher court with a judge and a jury.
fact: In old Rome, a magistrate was a person with public power, like a mayor or governor.
exercise: «The magistrate fined him for dropping litter.» What is a magistrate? | *A judge in a local court who decides smaller cases | A teacher who runs the school | A very large prison | A pilot who flies planes
exercise: What does the clue «only give short prison sentences of months, not years» tell you about magistrates? | *Magistrates cannot give very long prison sentences | Magistrates give the longest sentences of all | Magistrates never give any punishments | Magistrates only sentence people to years in prison
exercise: Mr Patel says, «I must go to the magistrates' court on Monday.» Where is he going? | To a shop to buy shoes | *To a local court where a judge decides cases | To a school to see his teacher
test: In the story, Toad is tried by magistrates and given twenty years. Why could this not really happen? | Magistrates always give twenty years | *Magistrates in a local court can only give short sentences, not years | Toad was not really in a story at all
test: Which word means a volunteer local judge, also called a Justice of the Peace? | Fine | Prisoner | Jury | *Magistrate
exam: What does «the magistrate fined him» show about a magistrate? | *It decides punishments, such as a fine | It only sells food in a shop | It is always a famous lawyer in a big city
